1
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:10,170
A games console costs 480 dollars.

2
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:14,140
In a sale, it is 5 sixths of the usual price.

3
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:15,660
What is the sale price?

4
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:17,250
Try to find a quick way.

5
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,770
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,430
5 sixths is the whole price, minus 1 sixth.

7
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:28,130
And 1 sixth of 480 is easy: it is 80.

8
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:30,360
480 minus 80 is 400.

9
00:00:30,410 --> 00:00:34,260
The sale price is 400 dollars.

10
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:35,860
Remember factors.

11
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:40,450
The factors of 12 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 12.

12
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,630
A number can be split into factors in different ways.

13
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,030
24 is 4 times 6, and also 3 times 8.

14
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:54,880
When a fraction is close to 1, find the small missing part, and subtract it from the whole.

15
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,620
9 tenths of 350.

16
00:00:56,670 --> 00:00:58,150
1 tenth is 35.

17
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:03,280
So 9 tenths is 350 minus 35, which is 315.

18
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:04,990
3 quarters of 96.

19
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:06,600
1 quarter is 24.

20
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:11,360
So 3 quarters is 96 minus 24, which is 72.

21
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:12,150
Your turn.

22
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,100
Work out 4 fifths of 650.

23
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:17,610
Pause the video and try it.

24
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,940
1 fifth of 650 is 130.

25
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:22,490
Take that away from 650.

26
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:24,960
The answer is 520.

27
00:01:25,010 --> 00:01:27,200
Here are three more ideas.

28
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:28,840
First: use factors.

29
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:31,770
1 twelfth is 1 third of 1 quarter.

30
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:36,710
So 1 twelfth of 600 is 1 third of 150, which is 50.

31
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:39,870
Second: cancel before you multiply.

32
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:48,890
In 15 over 28, times 14 over 45: 14 and 28 share a factor of 14, and 15 and 45 share a factor of 15.

33
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:54,030
That leaves 1 half times 1 third, which is 1 sixth.

34
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,430
Third: re-order.

35
00:01:55,480 --> 00:02:00,500
In 3 sevenths times 5 times 14, do 3 sevenths of 14 first.

36
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:01,380
That is 6.

37
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:03,770
Then 6 times 5 is 30.

38
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:05,130
Here is the method.

39
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,210
Step 1: look at the fraction.

40
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:08,420
Is it close to 1?

41
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:11,550
Then use whole minus the small part.

42
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:16,590
Step 2: look for common factors, and cancel before you multiply.

43
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:22,440
Step 3: split a denominator into factors, or re-order the multiplication.

44
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:25,250
Step 4: follow the order of operations.

45
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:29,250
Multiply and divide before you add and subtract.

46
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:32,700
Work out 11 twelfths of 840.

47
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:35,780
1 twelfth of 840 is 70.

48
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:39,020
840 minus 70 is 770.

49
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:42,360
Work out 1 fifteenth of 2,400.

50
00:02:42,410 --> 00:02:43,710
15 is 3 times 5.

51
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:47,960
So find 1 fifth first, then 1 third of that.

52
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:51,050
1 fifth of 2,400 is 480.

53
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:54,440
1 third of 480 is 160.

54
00:02:54,490 --> 00:02:55,280
Your turn.

55
00:02:55,330 --> 00:02:57,800
Work out 1 twentieth of 1,800.

56
00:02:57,850 --> 00:03:01,050
Pause and work it out.

57
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,160
20 is 10 times 2.

58
00:03:03,210 --> 00:03:06,130
1 tenth of 1,800 is 180.

59
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,900
Half of 180 is 90.

60
00:03:08,950 --> 00:03:13,500
Work out 18 over 25, times 35 over 36.

61
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:15,220
Cancel 18 and 36.

62
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:17,790
They become 1 and 2.

63
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,490
Cancel 35 and 25.

64
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:22,040
They become 7 and 5.

65
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:25,580
1 fifth times 7 halves is 7 tenths.

66
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:29,880
Work out 2 thirds, plus 1 third times 3 quarters.

67
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:31,090
Multiply first.

68
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:34,710
1 third times 3 quarters is 1 quarter.

69
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:35,430
Then add.

70
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:42,020
2 thirds plus 1 quarter is 8 twelfths plus 3 twelfths, which is 11 twelfths.

71
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:45,550
Ana works out 1 half, plus 1 half times 1 half.

72
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,590
Which line is wrong?

73
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,730
Line 1 is wrong.

74
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:49,860
Ana added first.

75
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:52,740
You must multiply before you add.

76
00:03:52,790 --> 00:03:55,430
1 half times 1 half is 1 quarter.

77
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:59,310
Then 1 half plus 1 quarter is 3 quarters.

78
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,970
You can use these tricks in any shop.

79
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:03,910
A sign says 10 percent off.

80
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:07,410
That means you pay 9 tenths of the price.

81
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:10,320
A pair of trainers costs 70 dollars.

82
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:12,570
1 tenth is 7 dollars.

83
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,120
70 minus 7 is 63.

84
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:15,860
You pay 63 dollars.

85
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:19,150
No written calculation needed.

86
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:20,480
One last question.

87
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:23,820
Work out 1 third, plus 2 thirds times 1 half.

88
00:04:23,870 --> 00:04:27,220
Pause the video and answer.

89
00:04:27,270 --> 00:04:28,430
Multiply first.

90
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,100
2 thirds times 1 half is 1 third.

91
00:04:31,150 --> 00:04:34,720
Then 1 third plus 1 third is 2 thirds.

92
00:04:34,770 --> 00:04:40,450
To remember: for a fraction close to 1, use the whole minus the small part.

93
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,940
Split denominators into factors.

94
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:46,140
1 twelfth is 1 third of 1 quarter.

95
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:50,470
Cancel before multiplying, and re-order when it helps.

96
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:53,930
And always follow the order of operations.

97
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:59,150
Great work! Now practise lesson 7.5 on Camday.
